{
    // plan.FinalPoints -> the most one raider may cost (StrengthOf), so a raid's own size
    // decides how well armed and armored its raiders are: a small or ramped raid is a few
    // cheap raiders, and elite gear and late bots come only with big raids. This is the only
    // gate on raider gear; raiders ignore the Days, Friendlies and SectorDifficulty
    // requirements of items (CombatRaid.RaiderGearSituation).
    // The popular colony sim's pirate curve with both axes divided by 10, since its cheapest
    // raider costs about 35 points and ours about 3.5. The value at 0 is also a floor, so the
    // cheapest raiders always fit. Raiders first fit, by price:
    //   ~10-11  a human with a rifle, Ion Disruptor or Vibroblade in a basic suit (70 points)
    //   ~16     a rifleman in a Combat Suit (140)
    //   ~18.7   a Sentry (170)
    //   ~24.7   an Orbotron (230)
    // See Docs/Architecture/Systems/RaidScaling.md, "Raider gear follows raid points".
    "FloatSet" : [
        0.0,    3.5,
        7.0,    5.0,
        70.0,   10.0,
        130.0,  15.0,
        300.0,  32.0,
        1000.0, 102.0
    ]
}
